Investigation Overview
1. Alert Summary and Trigger Analysis
The SIEM generated an alert triggered by a high volume of access attempts against the authentication endpoint (POST /accounts/login) using the account test@letsdefend.io. The traffic originated from an external IP address (134.209.145.73) located in a cloud region configured in the organization policy as Unused or Unsupported.

2. Threat Intelligence and Reputation Check (IOC Analysis)
Source IP: 134.209.145.73

Reputation Check (VirusTotal / AbuseIPDB): Verified as Malicious. The IP is flagged for active brute-force attacks, SSH scanning, and malicious web application probes.

Geofencing and Cloud Region: The IP originates from a restricted cloud infrastructure region in India.

3. Traffic and Impact Analysis
HTTP Request: POST /accounts/login HTTP/1.1

HTTP Status Code and Action: 403 Forbidden / Blocked

Log Correlation: Reviewing network and proxy logs confirmed that all incoming requests from 134.209.145.73 were successfully blocked by perimeter firewalls and security controls. No successful authentication or system compromise occurred.

Scope Determination: Search on SIEM and log management showed that only the target server (52.15.206.21) was targeted by this IP. No internal lateral movement or wider impact was observed.

Key Takeaways and Playbook Insights
Host Isolation Status: No Isolation Required

Rationale: Although the intent was malicious (True Positive), the firewall and proxy successfully dropped all requests (403 Blocked). The host was never compromised.

Defense Evasion Technique (T1535):

Attackers frequently leverage obscure or restricted cloud provider regions hoping that defenders lack proper logging or monitoring rules for traffic originating from those zones.
